  "notes": "Extracted from goma's actual gorilla/mux wiring - internal/router.go AddRoute/configureHandlers, internal/goma.go addGlobalHandler/registerMetricsHandler/registerRouteHealthHandler, internal/reload.go registerReloadHandler and the OAuth callback registered in internal/middleware.go - combined with every route path/host found in the built-in default config (internal/config.go), examples/, docs/ and the Go tests. Every YAML route becomes mux.PathPrefix(route.path).Subrouter() carrying an inner Host(h).PathPrefix(\"\") catch-all handler per configured host (or a single bare PathPrefix(\"\") when no hosts are set); per-route 'methods:' are enforced inside the proxy handler rather than by mux, so they are deliberately not modelled as gorilla method matchers here - only the global observability/reload endpoints really use .Methods().",
